WEBVTT

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:06.890
The first semester is almost over.

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:08.150
It's finally...

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:10.190
Summer vacation is coming up soon.

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:13.020
Please be careful, everyone.

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:14.700
Yahoo!

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.160
Summer vacation! A summer break!

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:21.700
That means no school!

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:24.810
Where should we go?

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:27.290
Vacation

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:32.340
Everyone! Make sure you spend every day to its fullest!

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:38.220
This is my first summer vacation with my boyfriend!

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:41.130
My first heartpounding experience...

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:45.890
Hey, are you gonna wear a yukata?

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:47.180
Of course!

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.420
I can't wait to check out the stands!

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:52.080
The fireworks festival this weekend!

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:55.100
I always go with my family, but...

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:57.900
Ayase Hanabi, age 12.

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:00.230
This year will be different.

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:06.020
I hope it'll be sunny that day.

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:07.200
Yep!

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:13.610
This year I will go on a fireworks date with my boyfriend for the first time!

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:59.950
Fireworks

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:03.880
Hanabi, you're going to the fireworks festival with Takao, right?

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:04.880
Yep!

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:08.750
That's nice! First the pool, now fireworks!

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:12.080
You're enjoying a couple's summer to its fullest!

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:13.090
That's great!

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:17.090
Will you be going with Hiyama, Yui?

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:20.960
Hiyama isn't going, I think.

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:22.750
Eh!?

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:30.310
The fireworks festival is this Saturday, right?

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:34.370
Y-Yes, um...

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:36.940
Would you like to go together?

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:40.860
I'm sorry. I can't go that day.

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:44.280
I need to help out at the bathhouse.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:45.790
Sorry!

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:49.540
It just can't be helped, then.

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:51.340
Yui turned into a stone!

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:55.820
Then would you like to come with us?

00:03:55.820 --> 00:03:57.080
No, that's fine.

00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:59.120
You've been waiting for this festival for a while.

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:00.270
But...

00:04:00.270 --> 00:04:03.600
Don't worry. I have cram school that day, too.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:06.230
Make sure to enjoy your date by yourselves.

00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:07.970
By ourselves...

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:11.750
Watching the fireworks while wearing your yukata...

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:13.540
By yourselves...

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:17.570
Your love will go buck wild! Bam!

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:19.250
Bam!

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:26.780
But my yukata is from 4th grade! Wouldn't it be too childish?

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:28.630
Don't worry.

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:31.320
Boys go crazy just seeing a girl in her yukata.

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:35.240
And I heard from my sis that a yukata makes you 30% more attractive!

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:39.580
Have you decided where to meet Takao?

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:42.180
Oh yeah, not yet...

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:45.210
Cocoa went to Tokyo the other day...

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:45.990
Takao...

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:50.640
Oh my, what business do you have?

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:51.700
Eikou...

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:54.500
You're going to the fireworks festival with Takao, right?

00:04:55.510 --> 00:04:58.510
Where will your couple's date be?

00:04:58.510 --> 00:05:02.790
You two haven't gone on a date by yourselves yet.

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:06.570
So pure.

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:08.200
Shut up!

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:10.160
We're going somewhere, okay?

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:16.930
If she spills her beans here, then Eikou and everyone will crash her date.

00:05:16.930 --> 00:05:18.950
This is a problem.

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:34.490
Takao...

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:39.670
Oh, don't mind us.

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:42.440
Why are you all here?

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:46.390
I can't talk to Takao like this!

00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:50.250
You don't have a cell phone, so you can't email him.

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:53.580
Let me try next!

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:55.710
The Rabbit Panda talked!

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:57.420
Rabbit Panda?

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:59.440
What's going on?

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:01.400
Oh, look at this!

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:05.260
So cute!

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:11.950
Hi, Hanabi.

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:14.640
You can record a message!

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:17.300
A message... Oh yeah!

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:25.590
Oh, has it started recording already?

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:29.120
Um... Uh... I'll wait for you at the park.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:43.280
So that's what happened.

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:45.550
It's not funny!

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:48.910
They've been following me around all day!

00:06:48.910 --> 00:06:50.790
Thanks, Ayase.

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:56.470
You didn't want anyone to bother us on our first date alone.

00:06:56.780 --> 00:06:57.840
Yeah.

00:06:57.840 --> 00:06:59.940
The fireworks start at seven...

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:06.080
How about we meet in front of the torii at 4 PM?

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:07.140
Yeah, sure...

00:07:07.140 --> 00:07:12.990
We'll start our date at 4 PM, right?

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:18.120
That's right, our date.

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:19.710
I can't wait for our date.

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:25.230
What do you want to eat on our date?

00:07:26.770 --> 00:07:29.290
You're too close, Takao.

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:31.640
Jeez!

00:07:33.350 --> 00:07:34.410
Hanabi...

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:37.740
I look forward to the fireworks festival. (Hanabi = Fireworks)

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:40.180
The first time we're alone.

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:44.690
Jeez, stop making fun of me.

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:49.060
I just can't wait for my date at the fireworks festival with my boyfriend!

00:07:49.950 --> 00:07:52.950
I want to eat shaved ice!

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:53.820
Okay.

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:58.020
And I want us to wear matching light-up watches!

00:07:58.020 --> 00:07:59.140
Okay.

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:17.590
So many people!

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:19.240
Um...

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:21.510
Something sparkling?

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:40.940
Ayase.

00:08:40.940 --> 00:08:43.880
Takao, your yukata...

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:46.710
Thank goodness. You're in a yukata, too.

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:50.680
What's wrong? Does it look weird?

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:52.390
Not at all.

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:55.220
Takao's yukata looks so cool!

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:58.780
Okay, let's go.

00:08:58.780 --> 00:08:59.840
Okay!

00:09:00.420 --> 00:09:03.380
Cram School

00:09:04.630 --> 00:09:08.100
We should be able to see the fireworks if we leave now.

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:10.370
Hey, hey, let's go together.

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:12.020
Want to come with us, Aoi?

00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:15.020
Sorry, I have somewhere I need to go.

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:31.480
My yukata seems a bit loose.

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:31.760
When you feel your sleeves going loose,

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:34.090
Marin's Advice

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:37.110
pull on the sash on your back,

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:39.680
stick your left hand into the sleeve,

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:42.230
and pull on the loose end.

00:09:42.230 --> 00:09:45.680
Then just adjust the sash in the front and you're done!

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:49.680
You gotta wear a beautiful yukata correctly or else you'll disappoint the boys.

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:51.500
Be careful of your sash, too.

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:54.520
It's hard to walk in a yukata.

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:59.030
When you're walking, take smaller steps.

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:01.410
Just take small steps.

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:07.910
Small steps...

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:13.400
What should I do? I'm getting left behind!

00:10:15.190 --> 00:10:18.070
Small steps... Small steps...

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:21.520
Did I walk a bit too fast?

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:23.900
Must be tough for a girl in a yukata.

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:29.720
There are so many people around, and I don't want to get separated.

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:35.070
Thank you.

00:10:37.980 --> 00:10:39.410
I'm sorry.

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:43.470
This is the first time I'm walking with a girl wearing a yukata.

00:10:44.110 --> 00:10:45.850
Takao...

00:10:47.110 --> 00:10:51.200
He said I'm his first! I'm kind of happy.

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:56.350
Why!? Why did it get away?

00:10:56.350 --> 00:10:58.700
You done, little mister?

00:10:58.700 --> 00:11:01.840
The ring is still here, even if the net's gone!

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:03.990
Become one with the goldfish!

00:11:03.990 --> 00:11:06.650
Challenge

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:11.130
What is Eikou doing?

00:11:11.300 --> 00:11:13.060
Shhh... He'll see us.

00:11:14.300 --> 00:11:17.290
They're selling light-up watches.

00:11:17.290 --> 00:11:19.360
You wanted one, right?

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:20.540
Let's go.

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:21.240
Okay!

00:11:22.020 --> 00:11:25.300
It's like a secret date!

00:11:28.690 --> 00:11:29.860
Okay.

00:11:30.980 --> 00:11:31.630
Off for today.

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:33.560
They're off!?

00:11:33.560 --> 00:11:35.940
What should I do?

00:11:35.940 --> 00:11:38.460
Do you need something from our house?

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:41.650
Your house? That means...

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:46.220
Don't tell me she's Hiyama's mom?

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:51.370
Um, is Hiyama here?

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:52.600
What's your name?

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:53.940
I'm Aoi Yui.

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:56.380
Are you Kazuma's girlfriend?

00:11:57.190 --> 00:12:02.040
No... I... Uh...

00:12:03.690 --> 00:12:04.950
Yes...

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:09.790
I wanted to see you!

00:12:17.020 --> 00:12:20.600
Kazuma, someone's here to see you.

00:12:22.060 --> 00:12:23.400
Aoi!?

00:12:23.400 --> 00:12:27.710
Jeez, you should have told me if your girlfriend was coming.

00:12:27.710 --> 00:12:28.780
Right?

00:12:28.780 --> 00:12:30.460
Jeez, you too.

00:12:31.130 --> 00:12:34.600
I'm in the way here, aren't I? Please enjoy yourselves.

00:12:34.600 --> 00:12:36.280
No, um...

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:39.530
Aoi, why?

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:42.050
I'm here to help.

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:44.990
Why? I told you it was fine.

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:47.120
You should go see the fireworks.

00:12:49.610 --> 00:12:51.680
But if it's not with you...

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:55.960
It's pretty tough, you know.

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:58.120
I'll do my best!

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:03.580
These are so cute!

00:13:03.580 --> 00:13:05.150
Yeah, it looks great.

00:13:05.150 --> 00:13:06.800
Then me too.

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:10.330
We're the same!

00:13:10.330 --> 00:13:12.680
I have to treasure this.

00:13:12.680 --> 00:13:15.730
Oh, these look pretty good.

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:16.940
Cocoa!?

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:18.700
Hanabi?

00:13:18.700 --> 00:13:20.210
So that means...

00:13:20.210 --> 00:13:22.170
Takao!

00:13:22.170 --> 00:13:25.480
Wow, what a coincidence?

00:13:25.480 --> 00:13:28.300
No wait, it's not really a coincidence?

00:13:28.300 --> 00:13:31.160
This is fate!

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:35.420
Takao, let's go see the fireworks together. Okay? Okay?

00:13:35.420 --> 00:13:36.480
No.

00:13:38.550 --> 00:13:40.790
Hanabi, it's fine, right?

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:42.190
Uh...

00:13:42.190 --> 00:13:43.540
What?

00:13:43.540 --> 00:13:46.760
You want to keep Takao all to yourself?

00:13:47.740 --> 00:13:49.700
Takao!

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:52.470
Ayase Hanabi, age 12.

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:57.760
This should have been our first date alone...

00:14:08.600 --> 00:14:11.510
Come on, Takao. Let's go.

00:14:11.510 --> 00:14:13.550
My yukata...

00:14:13.550 --> 00:14:16.600
Sorry, but the fireworks are starting. I'll listen some other time.

00:14:16.600 --> 00:14:17.280
Eh?

00:14:17.280 --> 00:14:18.790
Let's go, Ayase.

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:20.750
O-Okay.

00:14:23.440 --> 00:14:28.220
So they just have to be alone, huh?

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:32.230
What are you doing, Cocoa?

00:14:32.230 --> 00:14:34.890
I'm sorry, Hanabi.

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:36.790
What?

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:42.000
Oh! It's Takao!

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:44.320
Found him! He's wearing a yukata!

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:45.750
So cool!

00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:47.710
Found the real couple!

00:14:47.710 --> 00:14:50.850
Hamana! You're treating us to food here? For real?

00:14:50.850 --> 00:14:52.500
Thank you for the email!!

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:53.980
E-mail?

00:14:53.980 --> 00:14:56.900
Thanks for telling us, Cocoa.

00:14:56.900 --> 00:14:59.440
I won't let you two be alone.

00:14:59.440 --> 00:15:01.880
It's the Class 6-2 gathering!

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:03.920
Let's have fun together!

00:15:04.510 --> 00:15:06.980
I guess this is fine sometimes.

00:15:12.740 --> 00:15:15.070
Aoi, please wash over here.

00:15:15.070 --> 00:15:16.550
Okay.

00:15:18.510 --> 00:15:21.510
I wonder if Hanabi is enjoying her date?

00:15:24.810 --> 00:15:28.590
Our date alone just became...

00:15:28.960 --> 00:15:31.760
So you like green tea flavor?

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:33.180
How mature!

00:15:33.180 --> 00:15:35.120
I add all the flavors!

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:37.580
What a hero!

00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:40.520
It turned all black!

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:42.200
What greedy boys.

00:15:43.570 --> 00:15:47.180
Hanabi, your yukata is really cute.

00:15:47.180 --> 00:15:50.070
Really? I really like this one.

00:15:50.070 --> 00:15:53.600
It's so childish. Fits you perfectly.

00:15:53.600 --> 00:15:55.360
Huh? It's childish?

00:15:55.360 --> 00:15:59.920
I'm sure Takao is disappointed at seeing such a childish yukata.

00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:05.520
And I bought my yukata in Tokyo just for today.

00:16:10.840 --> 00:16:12.550
Ayase, your yukata.

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:15.270
Your sash is a bit loose.

00:16:15.270 --> 00:16:17.140
Oh no! What should I do?

00:16:17.140 --> 00:16:19.440
Don't worry. Leave it to me.

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:26.190
There.

00:16:26.190 --> 00:16:27.530
I'm sorry.

00:16:28.060 --> 00:16:31.700
My sash isn't even on right. I'm so useless.

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:36.410
I thought I could become cuter by wearing a yukata.

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:39.240
I'm sorry.

00:16:43.410 --> 00:16:46.520
I really was surprised seeing you like this today.

00:16:48.250 --> 00:16:51.110
You look so cute in a yukata, that's why.

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:54.410
Takao.

00:16:58.920 --> 00:17:01.240
The fireworks are starting soon.

00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:04.300
Takao! You can see them more clearly here.

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:07.400
Come on! Let's go!

00:17:09.170 --> 00:17:11.020
What's wrong?

00:17:11.020 --> 00:17:15.330
Sorry, I forgot something back there. Let me go find it.

00:17:15.330 --> 00:17:17.760
Eh? I'll go with you, then.

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:19.390
I'll go, too!

00:17:19.390 --> 00:17:24.340
You sure about that? We went to the shaved ice place... then the goldfish stall...

00:17:24.340 --> 00:17:26.700
Then the watch place.

00:17:26.700 --> 00:17:29.830
We also stopped by the cotton candy and the fried corn stalls...

00:17:29.830 --> 00:17:31.480
I'll wait for you here.

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:33.670
My feet hurts...

00:17:33.670 --> 00:17:35.940
Jeez, it's all the geta's fault.

00:17:35.940 --> 00:17:37.760
Then I'll be going now.

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:40.840
The fireworks are starting, so hurry up.

00:17:40.840 --> 00:17:45.960
Huh? What did he forget?

00:17:48.310 --> 00:17:50.190
Thank you.

00:17:51.730 --> 00:17:55.870
It's fireworks day and I'm sorry that you're here helping me out.

00:17:55.870 --> 00:18:00.020
It's fine. I want to be with you, that's why.

00:18:00.020 --> 00:18:04.130
But you're amazing, helping out at home.

00:18:05.030 --> 00:18:06.930
I have something I want.

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:11.800
They'll buy it for me if I help out at the bathhouse.

00:18:12.280 --> 00:18:14.600
What is it?

00:18:14.600 --> 00:18:16.900
Kazuma! Yui!

00:18:17.180 --> 00:18:19.590
The fireworks are starting!

00:18:23.870 --> 00:18:26.760
Huh? Did we come here?

00:18:26.760 --> 00:18:30.230
Did you lose something here?

00:18:30.230 --> 00:18:33.760
And what did you lose?

00:18:33.760 --> 00:18:36.160
Behind you, Ayase.

00:18:55.990 --> 00:18:57.950
So pretty!

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:03.270
Sorry! We have to look for what you lost!

00:19:03.270 --> 00:19:04.330
It's fine.

00:19:06.400 --> 00:19:12.200
What I lost is watching the fireworks with you alone, Ayase.

00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:20.740
Thank goodness you followed me or else I didn't know what to do.

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:28.410
I wanted to watch the fireworks with just you, Ayase.

00:19:40.510 --> 00:19:41.600
It's so pretty.

00:19:42.190 --> 00:19:43.530
Me, too.

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:45.410
What?

00:19:45.720 --> 00:19:47.680
Sorry, the fireworks are too loud.

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:52.210
I wanted to watch them with you alone, too.

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:00.140
They're so small.

00:20:00.140 --> 00:20:05.930
Not really. It's enough just to see them with you, Hiyama.

00:20:32.060 --> 00:20:33.820
It's over.

00:20:38.660 --> 00:20:41.490
I forgot to give this back to you.

00:20:41.490 --> 00:20:42.080
Oh!

00:20:49.330 --> 00:20:52.410
I want to watch them next year with you too, Hanabi.

00:20:53.450 --> 00:20:54.710
Takao?

00:20:56.020 --> 00:20:57.620
One more time!

00:20:57.620 --> 00:21:00.870
I want to watch them next year with you too, Hanabi.

00:21:00.870 --> 00:21:02.770
Whoa, stop doing that.

00:21:02.770 --> 00:21:02.880
I want to watch them next year with you too, Hanabi.

00:21:03.890 --> 00:21:05.150
Jeez.

00:21:05.150 --> 00:21:12.320
Is he talking about fireworks or my name?

00:21:15.010 --> 00:21:23.880
Next year... No, I want to keep on watching the fireworks with Takao forever!

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:27.220
Ayase Hanabi, age 12!

00:23:01.800 --> 00:23:03.200
Thank you for today.

00:23:03.200 --> 00:23:07.230
It's fine. Thank you for walking me home.

00:23:08.720 --> 00:23:10.980
You'll wear them next year, right?

00:23:10.980 --> 00:23:11.940
Huh?

00:23:13.560 --> 00:23:14.740
A yukata.

00:23:15.740 --> 00:23:16.810
Sure.

00:23:17.510 --> 00:23:19.500
Huh? Aoi?

00:23:19.500 --> 00:23:23.190
So it's true she got a boyfriend.

00:23:23.190 --> 00:23:27.310
So she can make such an expression.

00:23:27.310 --> 00:23:29.210
How cute.

00:23:32.630 --> 00:23:35.480
Aoi Yui, age 12.

00:23:35.480 --> 00:23:37.360
I feel a storm coming.

00:23:40.440 --> 00:23:45.230
12-sai Second Season is airing this October!

00:23:45.230 --> 00:23:48.280
There will be lots more of our boyfriend-girlfriend stories!

00:23:48.280 --> 00:23:52.060
A love rival appears and puts Yui and Hiyama in a huge pinch?

00:23:52.060 --> 00:23:57.410
And we'll be rerunning the first season starting in July!

00:23:57.410 --> 00:23:59.600
We'll make your hearts throb even more!
